making reportedly slow progress on major  fronts russia has widened its war on  ukraine  the missiles that fell on a military  training center near javorev in the far  west killed dozens soldiers and cadets  that russia claims were foreign trained  fighters preparing to enter the war  just a few months ago joint military  exercises took place here ukrainian  troops alongside allies from 14  countries yet now they're having to  fight and die in this war largely alone  scores more were injured in the most  devastating single attack so far and  with worrying implications for supply  routes delivering humanitarian and  military aid  the war has now come to western ukraine  and with it a sense that perhaps nowhere  in this country is safe  but of larger significance is the fact  that not just the country's main supply  routes are now vulnerable not just the  main avenues of escape for hundreds of  thousands of refugees have now become  vulnerable but the fact that the war has  now come  within 20 kilometers or so  of a nato border  in javorev on sunday morning anna woke  to the sound of explosions  i thought someone was breaking into the  house we went outside and the whole sky  was red  we met anna at a fuel stop a pregnant  daughter a niece and her grandchild in  the car making a dash for the polish  border  at home my sick father a husband and a  brother-in-law stayed behind  i would pick up arm myself and fight but  we have to save our children  and once again calls for nato to  intervene to enforce a no-fly zone over  ukraine  rockets have fallen 10 kilometers from  the border with europe  tomorrow they may fall 10 kilometers on  the other side in poland where our wives  and children are now i call on europe  save yourselves save us because tomorrow  it will be too late  but nato continues to have no appetite  to confront russia directly as the war  grinds on  in cities like cherny heap in the north  steady nerves required here  to remove an unwelcome delivery through  someone's front window  civilians those brave or desperate  enough to attempt escape continue to  leave areas close to kiev like erpin  where an american journalist was killed  when he and a colleague were fired on by  russian forces  and no respite yet again for mariopol  satellite images show swathes of  destruction in the southern city  besieged for two weeks the life being  strangled out of it an aid convoy once  again prevented from entering  there is one constant the inexhaustible  morale boosting russia-defying presence  of a comedian who once played the role  of president on tv now handing out  medals  and giving the performance of his life  jonah al jazeera yavariv
 

